RETRACTED 2026-09-17.

The multi-pass figures in size-sweep-padbean-20260917T123004Z.json are one measurement
repeated, not N measurements.

bench/size-sweep.sh shared a single run directory across passes. judge.sh names
its output attempt-N by counting the files already there, so pass 2 wrote
attempt-2 while the reader stayed pinned to attempt-1 — and the "did it answer?"
guard was file existence, which a previous pass satisfies, so a pass that
produced nothing was reported with the earlier pass's verdict.

Read the `points` array as ONE reading per size.

The clean re-run, with a fresh run directory per pass, is
size-sweep-clean-20260917T135317Z.json: 1 accept in 5 at 20,422 bytes and 1 in 5
at 40,422 — the same rate, and no size effect.

The file is kept unedited. A measurement is a record of what was believed and
when, and editing one to agree with a later one is how a project loses the
ability to say how it got where it is. This note sits beside it instead.
